{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers.md; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_go_build_cleanup_unix_test.go; git diff 7915719..b228d24 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json; sed -n '480,760p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go; cat pose-mcp/go.mod\"","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-14\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer a limpeza de uma execução de revisão delegada remover os diretórios de build do Go que um `go test` interrompido do revisor deixou no diretório de execução, para que uma revisão aprovada não seja recusada por limpeza incompleta.\n\n### Business value\nEm 2026-11-14 duas revisões seguidas da spec `pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets` foram aprovadas pelo Codex e recusadas pelo motor (\"the run's cleanup is not confirmed complete\"). O diretório de execução retido tinha 175 MB, acima do orçamento de 128 MiB do inventário de limpeza: 151 MB eram um `go-build*` com o binário de teste da CLI que o revisor compilou. A remoção desses diretórios existia só no wrapper do perfil de revisão do Claude; para qualquer outro adaptador, uma revisão que compila os testes da CLI esgota o orçamento e a run deixa de governar.\n\n### Constraints\n- O inventário limitado continua valendo para todo o resto do diretório de execução.\n- Um link com nome de `go-build*` nunca é seguido.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Não elevar o orçamento do inventário do diretório de execução.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: On Unix platforms, when a review run is cleaned up, every real directory named `go-build<digits>` at the top of its runtime directory shall be removed under its own bounded inventory before the runtime directory's inventory, for every adapter. On other platforms the go-build directory is left to the runtime inventory, unchanged from before this spec (follow-up F3).\n- R2: An entry named like one that is a link or not a directory shall be left to the runtime inventory, and its target shall never be touched.\n- R3: A go-build directory that exceeds its own bounded inventory, or that changes identity during cleanup, shall leave the cleanup incomplete, as any other unconfirmed cleanup.\n\n### Non-functional\n- Orçamento por diretório de build: 200.000 entradas e 8 GiB.\n\n### Security\n- A remoção usa a raiz do diretório de execução já capturada e confere a identidade do diretório aberto.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Nenhum formato muda.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/review_adapter_containment.go`: `removeReviewGoBuildLeftovers` antes do inventário do diretório de execução.\n\n### Artifacts\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_go_build_cleanup_unix.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_go_build_cleanup_other.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_go_build_cleanup_unix_test.go\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto por `pose delegate review`, cuja limpeza de execução chama esta remoção. Check permanente `review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestAdapterCleanupRemovesGoBuildLeftovers|TestAdapterContainmentCleanup' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Nenhum novo: o diretório removido é do Go, criado sob o TMPDIR que o motor dá à execução.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Remoção limitada dos `go-build*` de primeiro nível (R1, R2, R3).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Teste com um `go-build` de 200 MiB e 4.200 arquivos e um link com o mesmo padrão de nome; teste sincronizado de troca e sumiço do diretório depois de aberto.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nTeste de regressão sobre o fixture de limpeza de contenção existente; testes de contenção existentes.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-14\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26.\n- Notes: diretório retido da run `rrn-331ef7311adb902b`: 1.730 entradas, 175 MB, com `go-build4066122796` de 151 MB. Sem a mudança, o teste reprova com a mesma mensagem da recusa (\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\"); com ela, passa.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: limpeza completa com o leftover; link não seguido.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestAdapterCleanupRemovesGoBuildLeftovers test:TestReviewGoBuildEnumerationStopsAtTheBudget test:TestReviewGoBuildEnumerationDescriptorIsCloseOnExec test:TestGoBuildLeftoversDoNotCountAgainstTheRuntimeInventory check:review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestAdapterCleanupRemovesGoBuildLeftovers\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestAdapterCleanupRefusesAReplacedGoBuildDirectory test:TestAdapterCleanupRefusesAGoBuildReplacedBeforeRemoval test:TestAdapterCleanupDoesNotBlockOnAFIFOReplacement test:TestAdapterCleanupDoesNotBlockOnAFIFOBeforeTheFirstOpen test:TestAdapterCleanupRefusesANestedGoBuildDirectoryReplacedBeforeRemoval check:release-cross-build-windows check:release-cross-build-darwin check:release-test-compile-windows check:release-test-compile-darwin\n\n### Known gaps\n- Nenhuma.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nA limpeza de uma execução de revisão remove, com inventário limitado próprio, os diretórios de build do Go deixados no diretório de execução, para qualquer adaptador, sem seguir links.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n- `pose/review_adapter_containment.go`, teste de regressão, matriz.\n\n### Validation executed\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Result: verde.\n\n### Residual risks\n- Nenhum.\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] F1: abrir a raiz da execução e a worktree na limpeza de contenção de forma não bloqueante e exigindo diretório; `os.Root.OpenRoot` bloqueia se o nome for trocado por um FIFO entre a conferência e a abertura. Os diretórios `go-build` desta spec já não têm essa janela. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-12-13)\n- [open] F2: os testes de `internal/cli` não compilam para Windows (`syscall.Kill` em `delegate_mcp_test.go`, e o `go vet` para no primeiro erro de cada pacote); estender `release-test-compile-windows` ao módulo inteiro quando compilarem. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n- [open] F3: remover os diretórios `go-build` da limpeza também no Windows, com abertura relativa a handle e sem seguir reparse points; hoje ficam para o inventário da execução, como antes desta spec, e uma execução de revisão no Windows com um binário de teste grande continua com a limpeza incompleta. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n\n### Review\n\nRodada 1 (run rrn-11320f4eeb5bcde3, attestation rva-823ad7b9b9b0738b, changes-requested): 1 bloqueador, tratado. F1 a identidade do diretório de build só era conferida ao abri-lo: renomeado para fora e trocado por um vazio durante a limpeza, o substituto seria removido e a limpeza confirmada, e o sumiço era aceito em silêncio. Depois de esvaziá-lo, o nome tem de ligar ainda o mesmo diretório, ou a limpeza fica incompleta; um teste sincronizado cobre a troca e o sumiço. A ferramenta `validate` saiu reprovada só porque a reexecução no sandbox do revisor estourou 600 s; a evidência selada passou.\n\nRodada 2 (run rrn-78b11adc9ff36dd0, attestation rva-b65df389f4e7a242, changes-requested): o F1 ficou parcial e veio 1 bloqueador, tratado. N1 entre a última conferência do nome e a remoção, o diretório ainda podia ser trocado e a remoção do substituto confirmaria a limpeza. O diretório agora fica aberto durante a remoção, e só a confirmação, pelo descritor, de que ele ficou sem nenhum link (o original removido) confirma a limpeza; uma plataforma sem contagem de links não prova e recusa. Um teste sincronizado troca o diretório entre a conferência e a remoção.\n\nRodada 3 (run rrn-1a96cee8e24eb008): o motor recusou a conclusão porque o rascunho deu aos achados novos ids com prefixo de rodada (`R3-N1`); os dois achados foram tratados mesmo assim. N1 (alto) `syscall.Stat_t` num arquivo sem build tag não compila no Windows, alvo do release: a contagem de links passou para arquivos por plataforma (`unix` e o resto, que recusa), e a matriz ganhou os checks `release-cross-build-windows` e `release-cross-build-darwin`, cuja ausência deixou a rodada 2 passar a validação completa sem compilar para Windows. N2 a reabertura pelo nome (`root.Open`) bloqueava se o diretório fosse trocado por um FIFO: o diretório verificado fica aberto, sem reabertura, até a confirmação da remoção por ele; um teste sincronizado troca por um FIFO e exige o fim sem bloqueio. A janela entre a primeira conferência e a abertura é a da limpeza inteira (follow-up F1).\n\nRodada 4 (run rrn-67a184e6a36ce92e, attestation rva-fed978aec59d28de, changes-requested): os achados das rodadas anteriores estão corrigidos, e vieram 2 bloqueadores, tratados. N3 o teste do FIFO usava `syscall.Mkfifo` num arquivo de teste compilado também no Windows: os testes de FIFO foram para `review_go_build_cleanup_unix_test.go`, e a matriz ganhou `release-test-compile-windows` e `release-test-compile-darwin` (`go vet`, que compila os testes). N4 a primeira abertura (`OpenRoot`) ainda bloqueava num FIFO posto entre a listagem e a abertura: no Unix a remoção do `go-build` passou a ser toda feita por descritores (`openat` com `O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK` relativo ao descritor da raiz, `unlinkat` relativo ao descritor que contém a entrada, com inventário limitado), e o que não abre como diretório fica para o inventário da execução. Nas outras plataformas o `go-build` fica para esse inventário, que mantém a limpeza incompleta se exceder os limites. Um teste sincronizado troca por um FIFO antes da primeira abertura e exige o fim sem bloqueio.\n\nRodada 5 (run rrn-dfbb00c5cb708475, attestation rva-4ef3d3f9821cfeb3, changes-requested): N3 e N4 corrigidos, e vieram 4 bloqueadores, tratados. N5 a implementação fora do Unix não faz nada, e o R1 prometia a remoção em toda plataforma: o R1 foi restringido ao Unix, e o Windows ficou como follow-up F3, sem afirmar entrega que não há. N6 `Readdirnames(-1)` lia todas as entradas antes de consultar o limite: a leitura passou a ser em lotes de 256, cobrados do limite ao serem lidos, e o topo do diretório da execução também é lido em lotes, até o limite de 4.096 do inventário. N7 um diretório trocado ou sumido entre a listagem e a abertura era entregue ao inventário: a identidade lida antes da abertura liga o nome, e a troca deixa a limpeza incompleta; o teste agora exige esse erro. N8 `unix.Dup` tira o close-on-exec: a duplicação passou a ser `F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC`, atômica. Cada correção tem teste que reprova sem ela.\n\nRodada 6 (run rrn-18325d957ae046e0, attestation rva-2f60a62a1aaa0648, changes-requested): N6 a N8 corrigidos e N5 substituído pela emenda do R1; vieram 2 bloqueadores, tratados. N9 os subdiretórios eram removidos sem a confirmação feita no topo: toda remoção de diretório, em qualquer nível, passa por `unlinkReviewGoBuildBound`, que mantém o descritor aberto, confere o nome antes e exige, por ele, o original sem links depois. N10 o topo contava os `go-build` contra o limite de 4.096 do inventário de que eles saem antes: cada `go-build` é removido à medida que é lido, sem acumular nomes, e só as outras entradas contam. Um teste para cada um reprova sem a correção.\n\n     1\t//go:build unix\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\timport (\n     6\t\t\"fmt\"\n     7\t\n     8\t\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n     9\t\t\"os\"\n    10\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    11\t\t\"runtime\"\n    12\t\t\"syscall\"\n    13\t\t\"testing\"\n    14\t\t\"time\"\n    15\t)\n    16\t\n    17\t// Review round 3 (N2): a go-build directory replaced by a FIFO after it was\n    18\t// emptied leaves the cleanup incomplete without blocking: the verified\n    19\t// directory is never reopened by its name.\n    20\tfunc TestAdapterCleanupDoesNotBlockOnAFIFOReplacement(t *testing.T) {\n    21\t\tif runtime.GOOS != \"linux\" {\n    22\t\t\tt.Skip(\"Linux descriptor and symlink qualification\")\n    23\t\t}\n    24\t\tf := makeContainmentCleanupFixture(t)\n    25\t\tbuild := filepath.Join(f.tmp, \"go-build11\")\n    26\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(build, 0o700); err != nil {\n    27\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    28\t\t}\n    29\t\taway := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"away\")\n    30\t\toriginal := reviewGoBuildAfterContents\n    31\t\treviewGoBuildAfterContents = func(string) {\n    32\t\t\tif err := os.Rename(build, away); err != nil {\n    33\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n    34\t\t\t}\n    35\t\t\tif err := syscall.Mkfifo(build, 0o600); err != nil {\n    36\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n    37\t\t\t}\n    38\t\t}\n    39\t\tdefer func() { reviewGoBuildAfterContents = original }()\n    40\t\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n    41\t\tgo func() { done <- f.cleanup() }()\n    42\t\tselect {\n    43\t\tcase err := <-done:\n    44\t\t\tif err == nil {\n    45\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"cleanup was confirmed over a FIFO replacement\")\n    46\t\t\t}\n    47\t\tcase <-time.After(30 * time.Second):\n    48\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"cleanup blocked on a FIFO that replaced the go-build directory\")\n    49\t\t}\n    50\t}\n    51\t\n    52\t// Review rounds 4 and 5 (N4, N7): a go-build directory replaced by a FIFO\n    53\t// after it was listed and before it was first opened is not opened as one:\n    54\t// the cleanup ends without blocking, and incomplete.\n    55\tfunc TestAdapterCleanupDoesNotBlockOnAFIFOBeforeTheFirstOpen(t *testing.T) {\n    56\t\tif runtime.GOOS != \"linux\" {\n    57\t\t\tt.Skip(\"Linux descriptor and symlink qualification\")\n    58\t\t}\n    59\t\tf := makeContainmentCleanupFixture(t)\n    60\t\tbuild := filepath.Join(f.tmp, \"go-build13\")\n    61\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(build, 0o700); err != nil {\n    62\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    63\t\t}\n    64\t\taway := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"away\")\n    65\t\toriginal := reviewGoBuildBeforeOpen\n    66\t\treviewGoBuildBeforeOpen = func(string) {\n    67\t\t\tif err := os.Rename(build, away); err != nil {\n    68\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n    69\t\t\t}\n    70\t\t\tif err := syscall.Mkfifo(build, 0o600); err != nil {\n    71\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n    72\t\t\t}\n    73\t\t}\n    74\t\tdefer func() { reviewGoBuildBeforeOpen = original }()\n    75\t\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n    76\t\tgo func() { done <- f.cleanup() }()\n    77\t\tselect {\n    78\t\tcase err := <-done:\n    79\t\t\tif err == nil {\n    80\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"cleanup was confirmed after the go-build directory was replaced before its first open\")\n    81\t\t\t}\n    82\t\tcase <-time.After(30 * time.Second):\n    83\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"cleanup blocked on a FIFO that replaced the go-build directory before its first open\")\n    84\t\t}\n    85\t\tif info, err := os.Stat(away); err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n    86\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the renamed directory was lost: %v\", err)\n    87\t\t}\n    88\t}\n    89\t\n    90\t// Review round 5 (N8): the descriptor that enumerates a go-build directory\n    91\t// is close-on-exec, as every other descriptor of the cleanup.\n    92\tfunc TestReviewGoBuildEnumerationDescriptorIsCloseOnExec(t *testing.T) {\n    93\t\tdir := t.TempDir()\n    94\t\tdfd, err := unix.Open(dir, unix.O_RDONLY|unix.O_DIRECTORY|unix.O_CLOEXEC, 0)\n    95\t\tif err != nil {\n    96\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    97\t\t}\n    98\t\tdefer unix.Close(dfd)\n    99\t\tseen := -1\n   100\t\toriginal := reviewGoBuildEnumerating\n   101\t\treviewGoBuildEnumerating = func(fd int) {\n   102\t\t\tflags, err := unix.FcntlInt(uintptr(fd), unix.F_GETFD, 0)\n   103\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   104\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n   105\t\t\t}\n   106\t\t\tseen = flags & unix.FD_CLOEXEC\n   107\t\t}\n   108\t\tdefer func() { reviewGoBuildEnumerating = original }()\n   109\t\tbudget := reviewGoBuildBudget{entries: 10, bytes: 10}\n   110\t\tif err := removeReviewGoBuildContents(dfd, 0, &budget); err != nil {\n   111\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   112\t\t}\n   113\t\tif seen != unix.FD_CLOEXEC {\n   114\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"enumeration descriptor flags %d lack FD_CLOEXEC\", seen)\n   115\t\t}\n   116\t}\n   117\t\n   118\t// Review round 5 (N6): a go-build directory with more entries than its\n   119\t// budget is refused before all of them are read.\n   120\tfunc TestReviewGoBuildEnumerationStopsAtTheBudget(t *testing.T) {\n   121\t\tdir := t.TempDir()\n   122\t\tfor i := 0; i < 600; i++ {\n   123\t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, fmt.Sprintf(\"f%d\", i)), nil, 0o600); err != nil {\n   124\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   125\t\t\t}\n   126\t\t}\n   127\t\tdfd, err := unix.Open(dir, unix.O_RDONLY|unix.O_DIRECTORY|unix.O_CLOEXEC, 0)\n   128\t\tif err != nil {\n   129\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   130\t\t}\n   131\t\tdefer unix.Close(dfd)\n   132\t\tread := 0\n   133\t\toriginal := reviewGoBuildRead\n   134\t\treviewGoBuildRead = func(n int) { read += n }\n   135\t\tdefer func() { reviewGoBuildRead = original }()\n   136\t\tbudget := reviewGoBuildBudget{entries: 100, bytes: 1 << 20}\n   137\t\tif err := removeReviewGoBuildContents(dfd, 0, &budget); err == nil {\n   138\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"a directory over its entry budget was confirmed\")\n   139\t\t}\n   140\t\tif read > 256 {\n   141\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"enumeration read %d entries of 600 before refusing a budget of 100\", read)\n   142\t\t}\n   143\t}\n   144\t\n   145\t// Review round 6 (N9): a nested directory of a go-build tree renamed away\n   146\t// and replaced between the check of its name and its removal leaves the\n   147\t// cleanup incomplete, and the renamed directory is not lost.\n   148\tfunc TestAdapterCleanupRefusesANestedGoBuildDirectoryReplacedBeforeRemoval(t *testing.T) {\n   149\t\tif runtime.GOOS != \"linux\" {\n   150\t\t\tt.Skip(\"Linux descriptor and symlink qualification\")\n   151\t\t}\n   152\t\tf := makeContainmentCleanupFixture(t)\n   153\t\tnested := filepath.Join(f.tmp, \"go-build15\", \"b001\")\n   154\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(nested, 0o700); err != nil {\n   155\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   156\t\t}\n   157\t\taway := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"away\")\n   158\t\toriginal := reviewGoBuildNestedBeforeRemove\n   159\t\treviewGoBuildNestedBeforeRemove = func(string) {\n   160\t\t\tif err := os.Rename(nested, away); err != nil {\n   161\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n   162\t\t\t}\n   163\t\t\tif err := os.Mkdir(nested, 0o700); err != nil {\n   164\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n   165\t\t\t}\n   166\t\t}\n   167\t\tdefer func() { reviewGoBuildNestedBeforeRemove = original }()\n   168\t\tif err := f.cleanup(); err == nil {\n   169\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"removing a nested replacement confirmed the go-build cleanup\")\n   170\t\t}\n   171\t\tif info, err := os.Stat(away); err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n   172\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the renamed directory was lost: %v\", err)\n   173\t\t}\n   174\t}\n   175\t\n   176\t// Review round 6 (N10): go-build directories do not count against the\n   177\t// runtime inventory they are removed before: a runtime with exactly as many\n   178\t// other entries as that inventory admits, plus go-build directories, is\n   179\t// cleaned up.\n   180\tfunc TestGoBuildLeftoversDoNotCountAgainstTheRuntimeInventory(t *testing.T) {\n   181\t\tdir := t.TempDir()\n   182\t\tfor i := 0; i < reviewRuntimeMaxEntries; i++ {\n   183\t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, fmt.Sprintf(\"f%04d\", i)), nil, 0o600); err != nil {\n   184\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   185\t\t\t}\n   186\t\t}\n   187\t\tfor i := 0; i < 3; i++ {\n   188\t\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(dir, fmt.Sprintf(\"go-build%d\", i), \"b001\"), 0o700); err != nil {\n   189\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   190\t\t\t}\n   191\t\t}\n   192\t\troot, err := os.OpenRoot(dir)\n   193\t\tif err != nil {\n   194\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   195\t\t}\n   196\t\tdefer root.Close()\n   197\t\tif err := removeReviewGoBuildLeftovers(root); err != nil {\n   198\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"go-build directories counted against the runtime inventory: %v\", err)\n   199\t\t}\n   200\t\tif err := removeReviewOwnedContents(root, reviewRuntimeMaxEntries, 128<<20); err != nil {\n   201\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the runtime inventory refused what it admits: %v\", err)\n   202\t\t}\n   203\t\tleft, err := os.ReadDir(dir)\n   204\t\tif err != nil || len(left) != 0 {\n   205\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"runtime not emptied: %d entries, %v\", len(left), err)\n   206\t\t}\n   207\t}\ndiff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex c7afbb15..7f5c3015 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2398,6 +2398,57 @@\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers-integration\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/pose\", \"-run\", \"TestAdapterCleanupRemovesGoBuildLeftovers|TestAdapterContainmentCleanup\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"release-cross-build-windows\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"build\", \"-o\", \"/dev/null\", \"./cmd/pose\"],\n+          \"env\": {\n+            \"GOOS\": \"windows\",\n+            \"GOARCH\": \"amd64\"\n+          },\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"build\"\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"release-cross-build-darwin\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"build\", \"-o\", \"/dev/null\", \"./cmd/pose\"],\n+          \"env\": {\n+            \"GOOS\": \"darwin\",\n+            \"GOARCH\": \"arm64\"\n+          },\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"build\"\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"release-test-compile-windows\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"vet\", \"./internal/pose\"],\n+          \"env\": {\n+            \"GOOS\": \"windows\",\n+            \"GOARCH\": \"amd64\"\n+          },\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"build\"\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"release-test-compile-darwin\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"vet\", \"./...\"],\n+          \"env\": {\n+            \"GOOS\": \"darwin\",\n+            \"GOARCH\": \"arm64\"\n+          },\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"build\"\n+        },\n         {\n           \"name\": \"milestone-closes-when-reached-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\nindex 8a957a0e..b2223b75 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\n@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@ package pose\n \n import (\n \t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"fmt\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n@@ -326,3 +328,115 @@ func TestAdapterContainmentEscapedFiniteChildIsDisclosedNotContained(t *testing.\n \t}\n \tt.Fatal(\"escape fixture did not exercise the disclosed limitation\")\n }\n+\n+// Spec pose-review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers: the Go build directory\n+// an interrupted reviewer test left in the runtime directory is removed even\n+// when it alone exceeds the runtime inventory, and a link named like one is\n+// never followed.\n+func TestAdapterCleanupRemovesGoBuildLeftovers(t *testing.T) {\n+\tif runtime.GOOS != \"linux\" {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"Linux descriptor and symlink qualification\")\n+\t}\n+\tf := makeContainmentCleanupFixture(t)\n+\tbuild := filepath.Join(f.tmp, \"go-build4066122796\")\n+\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(build, \"b001\"), 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tbig := filepath.Join(build, \"b001\", \"cli.test\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(big, nil, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.Truncate(big, 200<<20); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 4200; i++ {\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(build, fmt.Sprintf(\"obj%04d.a\", i)), []byte(\"x\"), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\toutside := t.TempDir()\n+\tkeep := filepath.Join(outside, \"keep\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(keep, []byte(\"outside\"), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.Symlink(outside, filepath.Join(f.tmp, \"go-build1\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := f.cleanup(); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a go-build leftover kept the run from cleaning up: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := os.Lstat(f.tmp); !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the runtime directory remains: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif raw, err := os.ReadFile(keep); err != nil || string(raw) != \"outside\" {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a go-build link was followed out of the runtime: %v %q\", err, raw)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// Review round 1 (F1): a go-build directory renamed away and replaced after\n+// it was opened leaves the cleanup incomplete, and the renamed directory is\n+// not lost.\n+func TestAdapterCleanupRefusesAReplacedGoBuildDirectory(t *testing.T) {\n+\tif runtime.GOOS != \"linux\" {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"Linux descriptor and symlink qualification\")\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, change := range []string{\"replaced\", \"removed\"} {\n+\t\tt.Run(change, func(t *testing.T) {\n+\t\t\tf := makeContainmentCleanupFixture(t)\n+\t\t\tbuild := filepath.Join(f.tmp, \"go-build7\")\n+\t\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(build, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\taway := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"away\")\n+\t\t\toriginal := reviewGoBuildAfterContents\n+\t\t\treviewGoBuildAfterContents = func(name string) {\n+\t\t\t\tif err := os.Rename(build, away); err != nil {\n+\t\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n+\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\tif change == \"replaced\" {\n+\t\t\t\t\tif err := os.Mkdir(build, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n+\t\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tdefer func() { reviewGoBuildAfterContents = original }()\n+\t\t\tif err := f.cleanup(); err == nil {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"cleanup was confirmed after the go-build directory changed\")\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif info, err := os.Stat(away); err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the renamed directory was lost: %v\", err)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t})\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// Review round 2 (N1): a go-build directory renamed away and replaced after\n+// the last check of its name, just before its removal, leaves the cleanup\n+// incomplete; the removal of the replacement does not confirm it.\n+func TestAdapterCleanupRefusesAGoBuildReplacedBeforeRemoval(t *testing.T) {\n+\tif runtime.GOOS != \"linux\" {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"Linux descriptor and symlink qualification\")\n+\t}\n+\tf := makeContainmentCleanupFixture(t)\n+\tbuild := filepath.Join(f.tmp, \"go-build9\")\n+\tif err := os.MkdirAll(build, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\taway := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"away\")\n+\toriginal := reviewGoBuildBeforeRemove\n+\treviewGoBuildBeforeRemove = func(string) {\n+\t\tif err := os.Rename(build, away); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif err := os.Mkdir(build, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Error(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tdefer func() { reviewGoBuildBeforeRemove = original }()\n+\tif err := f.cleanup(); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"removing a replacement confirmed the go-build cleanup\")\n+\t}\n+\tif info, err := os.Stat(away); err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the renamed directory was lost: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n\nfunc (s Store) cleanupReviewResources(tmp string, owned os.FileInfo, worktree string, worktreeOwned os.FileInfo, gitMarker []byte, ownership ...*reviewCleanupOwnership) error {\n\tvar o *reviewCleanupOwnership\n\tif len(ownership) > 0 {\n\t\to = ownership[0]\n\t}\n\tcurrent, err := os.Lstat(tmp)\n\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\tif (o != nil && !o.removed) || (o == nil && worktreeOwned != nil) {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime path disappeared without confirmed cleanup; resources may remain\")\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tif err != nil || !current.IsDir() || !os.SameFile(owned, current) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup refused: runtime directory identity changed\")\n\t}\n\n\tvar root *os.Root\n\tif o != nil {\n\t\troot = o.runtime\n\t} else {\n\t\troot, err = os.OpenRoot(tmp)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup root unavailable\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer root.Close()\n\t}\n\tstat, err := root.Stat(\".\")\n\tif err != nil || !os.SameFile(owned, stat) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup root identity changed\")\n\t}\n\tif worktreeOwned != nil {\n\t\tinfo, err := root.Lstat(\"worktree\")\n\t\tif err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup unavailable\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err == nil {\n\t\t\tmarker, e := readReviewRootFile(root, \"worktree/.git\", 4096)\n\t\t\tif e != nil || !info.IsDir() || !os.SameFile(worktreeOwned, info) || !bytes.Equal(marker, gitMarker) {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup refused: worktree identity changed\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif o == nil || o.registry == nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration ownership unavailable; resources retained\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tinfo, e := o.registry.Lstat(o.registration)\n\t\tif e != nil || !info.IsDir() || !os.SameFile(info, o.registrationInfo) {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration identity changed\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tregistration, e := o.registry.OpenRoot(o.registration)\n\t\tif e != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration unavailable\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer registration.Close()\n\t\tinfo, e = registration.Stat(\".\")\n\t\tif e != nil || !os.SameFile(info, o.registrationInfo) {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration identity changed\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tbacklink, e := readReviewRootFile(registration, \"gitdir\", 4096)\n\t\tif e != nil || strings.TrimSpace(string(backlink)) != o.backlink {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration backlink changed\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, lock := range []string{\"locked\", \"index.lock\", \"HEAD.lock\"} {\n\t\t\tif _, e := registration.Lstat(lock); !errors.Is(e, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree registration has a live or unknown lock; resources retained\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err == nil {\n\t\t\ttree, e := root.OpenRoot(\"worktree\")\n\t\t\tif e != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup root unavailable\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tinfo, e := tree.Stat(\".\")\n\t\t\tif e != nil || !os.SameFile(info, worktreeOwned) {\n\t\t\t\ttree.Close()\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup identity changed\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\te = removeReviewOwnedContents(tree, 100000, 256<<20)\n\t\t\ttree.Close()\n\t\t\tif e != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn e\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif e := root.Remove(\"worktree\"); e != nil && !errors.Is(e, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup incomplete\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif e := removeReviewOwnedContents(registration, 1024, 256<<20); e != nil {\n\t\t\treturn e\n\t\t}\n\t\tregistration.Close()\n\t\tif e := o.registry.Remove(o.registration); e != nil && !errors.Is(e, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree registration cleanup incomplete\")\n\t\t}\n\t} else if _, e := root.Lstat(\"worktree\"); !errors.Is(e, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"partial worktree setup has no verified ownership; resources retained\")\n\t}\n\tif err := removeReviewGoBuildLeftovers(root); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif err := removeReviewOwnedContents(root, reviewRuntimeMaxEntries, 128<<20); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tcurrent, err = os.Lstat(tmp)\n\tif err != nil || !os.SameFile(owned, current) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime path changed during cleanup; replacement retained\")\n\t}\n\tif err := os.Remove(tmp); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime directory cleanup incomplete\")\n\t}\n\tif o != nil {\n\t\to.removed = true\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// reviewGoBuildDir names the temporary build directory the Go toolchain\n// creates under the TMPDIR the engine gives a review run.\nvar reviewGoBuildDir = regexp.MustCompile(`^go-build[0-9]+$`)\n\n// reviewGoBuildBeforeOpen runs after a go-build name is listed and before it\n// is opened, reviewGoBuildAfterContents after the directory is emptied and\n// before its name is checked again, and reviewGoBuildBeforeRemove between that\n// check and the removal; tests use them to change the name there.\nvar (\n\treviewGoBuildBeforeOpen    = func(string) {}\n\treviewGoBuildAfterContents = func(string) {}\n\treviewGoBuildBeforeRemove  = func(string) {}\n)\n\n// removeReviewGoBuildLeftovers removes the Go build directories a reviewer's\n// interrupted `go test` or `go build` left at the top of the run's runtime\n// directory, each under its own bounded inventory, before the runtime's own\n// inventory, which a single test binary can exceed (spec\n// pose-review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers). Only a real directory is\n// removed; the platform implementation opens it without blocking and only as\n// a directory, so a link, a FIFO or any other entry stays for the runtime\n// inventory to judge.\nfunc removeReviewGoBuildLeftovers(root *os.Root) error {\n\t// The top level is read in bounded batches and each go-build directory\n\t// is removed as it is read, so nothing accumulates; only the other\n\t// entries, which the runtime inventory will judge, count against its\n\t// bound (review rounds 5 and 6, N6 and N10).\n\tdir, err := root.Open(\".\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\")\n\t}\n\tdefer dir.Close()\n\tothers := 0\n\tfor {\n\t\tbatch, err := dir.Readdirnames(256)\n\t\tfor _, name := range batch {\n\t\t\tif !reviewGoBuildDir.MatchString(name) {\n\t\t\t\tothers++\n\t\t\t\tif others > reviewRuntimeMaxEntries {\n\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\")\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif err := removeReviewGoBuildDir(root, name); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(batch) == 0 {\n\t\t\tif err == nil || errors.Is(err, io.EOF) {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// reviewRuntimeMaxEntries is the runtime inventory's own entry bound.\nconst reviewRuntimeMaxEntries = 4096\n\nfunc removeReviewOwnedContents(root *os.Root, maxFiles int, maxBytes int64) error {\n\tpaths := []string{}\n\tvar total int64\n\terr := fs.WalkDir(root.FS(), \".\", func(path string, d fs.DirEntry, err error) error {\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif path == \".\" {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(paths) >= maxFiles || strings.Count(path, \"/\") > 128 {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup inventory exceeds coverage\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tinfo, err := d.Info()\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif info.Mode().IsRegular() {\n\t\t\ttotal += info.Size()\n\t\t\tif total > maxBytes {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup inventory exceeds bytes\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tpaths = append(paths, path)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\")\n\t}\n\tfor i := len(paths) - 1; i >= 0; i-- {\n\t\tif err := root.Remove(paths[i]); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup incomplete; resources retained\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc reviewSafetyConflict(run ReviewRun) string {\n\tif run.Safety == nil {\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t} // Historical runs have no invented observations.\n\tif run.Safety.SchemaVersion != 1 || (run.Status == ReviewRunCompleted && !run.Safety.CaptureComplete) {\n\t\treturn \"adapter capture incomplete\"\n\t}\n\tif run.Safety.Operation.Outcome != OutcomeCompleted {\n\t\treturn \"adapter cleanup incomplete\"\n\t}\n\treturn \"\"\n}\n\nfunc existingReviewDispatchResult(run ReviewRun) (ReviewRun, error) {\n\tif run.Safety != nil && run.Safety.Operation.Outcome != OutcomeCompleted {\n\t\treturn run, fmt.Errorf(\"existing dispatch has incomplete cleanup; no new adapter was started\")\n\t}\n\treturn run, nil\n}\nmodule github.com/harne8/pose-mcp\n\ngo 1.26.0\n\nrequire (\n\tgithub.com/harne8/mcp-enforce v0.0.0\n\tgithub.com/redis/go-redis/v9 v9.22.0\n\tgithub.com/yuin/goldmark v1.8.4\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlpmetric/otlpmetrichttp v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace v1.47.0\n\tgolang.org/x/sys v0.48.0\n)\n\nrequire (\n\tgithub.com/cenkalti/backoff/v5 v5.0.3 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/cespare/xxhash/v2 v2.3.0 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/go-logr/logr v1.4.4 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/go-logr/stdr v1.2.2 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/google/uuid v1.6.0 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/grpc-ecosystem/grpc-gateway/v2 v2.30.0 // indirect\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/auto/sdk v1.2.1 // indirect\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace v1.47.0 // indirect\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/log v1.47.0 // indirect\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/proto/otlp v1.11.0 // indirect\n\tgo.uber.org/atomic v1.11.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/net v0.60.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/text v0.42.0 // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/api v0.0.0-20260928230214-8a89bd6388cc // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/rpc v0.0.0-20260928230214-8a89bd6388cc // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/grpc v1.83.2 // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/protobuf v1.36.12 // indirect\n)\n\nreplace github.com/harne8/mcp-enforce => ../mcp-enforce\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
